  "notes": [
    "Every request that Rust accepts matches the pinned Go engine on the whole result and the first-fight log: 56 of 72.",
    "The 16 rejected requests are the tank builds (Protection, Holy Protection and Ret Protection Paladin, Feral bear Druid), refused by the exporter because Go has every copy of the boss swing at the tank, which Rust does not simulate. The same bear without its tank assignment is among the matches.",
    "The application's own builds helper (tools/reference-capture/builds) needs the application's worker module, which was not available, so the requests copy the boss in the production reference requests and add the area and multidot lines by hand rather than the lines the application adds; they exercise the same Go and Rust paths.",
    "Before the multidot fixes, a multidot line for Moonfire and Insect Swarm gave a Balance Druid 14 DPS against Go's 644 at 3 targets, a line for Rake and Rip a Feral cat 321 against 503, and a line for Consecration a Retribution Paladin 873 against 812; those variants are in this record and now match."
